  "section_path_text": "Force Majeure In France",
  "level": 0,
  "ordinal": 0,
  "summary": "What are the implications for tanker demand? After the oil industry suffered from a severe drought in Venezuela, forest fires in Canada and rebel attacks on oil installations in Nigeria, it is now facing the consequences of a national strike in France, where members of the trade union CGT have organized strikes at the country's refineries and blocked oil terminals and fuel depots. The situation seems to be worsening as more unions join the CGT and clashes break out between protestors and the police.",
